---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/url';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, NETWORK_NAME } from '../../../site.config.mjs';

const LAST_UPDATED = '7 October 2026';
---

<SiteLayout title="Privacy and terms">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12 md:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl">Privacy and terms</h1>

    <div class="prose-page">
      <h2>Privacy notice</h2>
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

      <h3>Who we are</h3>
      <p>
        The {NETWORK_NAME} (“the network”, “we” or “us”) is managed by a volunteer leadership committee comprising
        researchers from participating universities, research institutes and other organisations.
      </p>
      <p>
        The committee oversees this website, the directory and membership administration. Committee members’ institutional
        affiliations identify where they work; they do not, by themselves, mean those institutions operate the website.
      </p>
      <p>For privacy questions or requests, contact <strong>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</strong>.</p>

      <h3>What we collect</h3>
      <p>
        We collect information you provide when you submit a listing, request membership, share a resource, send a
        message or contact us. This may include:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Dataset listings:</strong> a description of the dataset, information about its availability and
          conditions of access, the lead institution, and the contact person’s name, role and email address.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Skills profiles:</strong> your name, title, role, career stage, institution, state or territory,
          discipline, skills, biography, ORCID iD, profile link, collaboration interests and email address.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Membership requests:</strong> your name, email address, institution, country, role and, if you choose
          to tell us, how you intend to use the network.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Messages and enquiries:</strong> your name, email address, institution, the topic you choose and your
          message when you use a contact form, and any correspondence you send to the network’s email address.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Shared resources:</strong> the materials you contribute, your name and email address, and any licence or
          conditions of use you provide.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>News and events posts:</strong> the details of the item you share, and your name and email address.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Sign-in:</strong> your email address, and the date and time you last signed in.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Our directory collects descriptions of research datasets, not the datasets themselves. Do not submit participant
        data, completed consent forms or information that could identify a study participant.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you provide another person’s details, you must have their permission to share those details for the purposes
        described in this notice.
      </p>

      <h3>Why we collect and use information</h3>
      <p>We use information to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Review, publish and maintain dataset listings and skills profiles.</li>
        <li>Help people connect about research, clinical practice, policy, education and collaboration.</li>
        <li>Deliver messages to the person you wish to contact.</li>
        <li>Assess membership requests and manage access to member resources.</li>
        <li>Contact contributors about submissions, corrections and periodic reviews.</li>
        <li>Respond to enquiries, privacy requests and complaints.</li>
        <li>Moderate content and address misuse of the website.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can browse the public directory without submitting a listing or becoming a member. Some activities require
        contact details so we can administer your request or enable a reply.
      </p>

      <h3>What is public and what is private</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Approved directory listings are public.</strong> For datasets, this is the dataset description, access
        information, lead institution, and the contact person’s name and role. For skills profiles, it is everything you
        submit for publication except your email address.
      </p>
      <p>
        Email addresses entered in the email fields are never displayed on the website. Avoid including an email address
        or other private information in a public description or biography.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Member resources</strong> are visible only to approved members, who see each resource and the name of the
        person who shared it. The sharer’s email address is visible only to network administrators.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Approved news and events posts are public</strong>, unless marked members only. The name and email address
        of the person who posted them are visible only to network administrators.
      </p>
      <p>
        Pending submissions, proposed updates, membership applications and internal review notes are never published.
        Authorised network administrators can access the information needed to review submissions and administer the
        network. The service providers listed below process information needed to operate the website and email.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you send a message through the website, we collect your name, email address, institution, the topic you
        choose and your message. Network administrators can see messages so they can block spam or misuse. We then pass
        the message to the person you contact, so they can reply to you directly; their reply goes straight to you, and
        the network does not see it. Once delivered, your message is held in the recipient’s own email account, and how
        long they keep it is up to them and their organisation. We cannot delete it from their account.
      </p>
      <p>
        Public listings may be viewed internationally, indexed by search engines or copied by others. Removing a listing
        from our website does not necessarily remove copies held elsewhere.
      </p>

      <h3>Service providers and overseas processing</h3>
      <p>We use these services to run the website. Some of them may process information outside Australia.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Supabase</strong> stores the database (listings, messages, membership records and sign-in accounts) and
          members’ resource files. Our project is hosted in Sydney, Australia. Supabase is based in the United States and
          may process some operational information, such as service logs and support requests, in other countries.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>GitHub</strong> (United States) hosts the website, runs our automated email and backup tasks, and stores
          our weekly backups in a private repository. Backups include email addresses and other information held in the
          database.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google</strong> (Gmail) sends the website’s emails from the network’s email account, which keeps copies
          of sent emails. Google may store this information outside Australia.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If you contact someone outside Australia through the directory, the information in your message will also be sent
        to that recipient overseas.
      </p>

      <h3>Cookies and technical information</h3>
      <p>
        We do not use advertising or analytics tools, or tracking cookies. When you sign in, your browser stores a sign-in
        session so you stay signed in until you sign out. The website’s fonts are hosted with the website, so no requests
        are made to font services.
      </p>
      <p>
        We count how many times each dataset and profile page is viewed, and show these counts only to the listing’s
        owner and to administrators. The count does not identify anyone. So that the same visit isn’t counted twice in a
        day, your browser keeps a small note of the listings you have viewed that day.
      </p>
      <p>
        For YouTube recordings shared with members, our automated task copies the video’s thumbnail image from YouTube
        into our own storage, so your browser does not contact YouTube when you view the Resources page.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our hosting providers (GitHub and Supabase) may record technical information, such as IP addresses and access
        logs, to operate and secure their services.
      </p>

      <h3>How long we keep information</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Published listings</strong> are kept while they are published. Each year we ask the owner to confirm they are still current.</li>
        <li><strong>Rejected and withdrawn listings</strong> are deleted automatically 12 months after the decision or withdrawal.</li>
        <li><strong>Membership records</strong> are kept while the membership is active. Declined requests and ended memberships are deleted 12 months later.</li>
        <li><strong>Messages sent through the website</strong> are deleted from our database after 12 months.</li>
        <li><strong>News and events posts</strong> stay in the public archive once published. Rejected and removed posts are deleted 12 months later.</li>
        <li><strong>View counts</strong> contain no personal information and are kept while the listing exists.</li>
        <li><strong>Copies of emails</strong> in the network’s email account are deleted after about 12 months.</li>
        <li><strong>Sign-in accounts</strong> (your email address and sign-in dates) are kept until you ask us to remove them.</li>
        <li><strong>Backups</strong> are kept for about 8 weeks, then permanently removed.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Withdrawing a listing removes it from public display straight away. The underlying record is then deleted on the
        schedule above.
      </p>

      <h3>Access, corrections and removal</h3>
      <p>
        You can update or withdraw your own listing at any time by <a href={withBase('/account/')}>signing in</a> with the
        email address on the listing. You can also request access to your personal information, ask for a correction, or
        request removal of your listing or closure of your membership by emailing <strong>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may ask for information to verify your identity before acting on a request. If we cannot fulfil a request in
        full, we will explain why and describe any available alternatives.
      </p>
      <p>
        Contributors are responsible for keeping their submissions accurate and current. Please also tell us if you
        believe information about you has been published incorrectly or without permission.
      </p>

      <h3>Privacy concerns and complaints</h3>
      <p>
        Contact <strong>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</strong> with any concern about how the network handles your personal
        information. Explain the issue and the outcome you are seeking, without including unnecessary sensitive
        information.
      </p>
      <p>We aim to respond within 30 days. If more time is needed, we will let you know.</p>
      <p>
        If the matter remains unresolved, you can seek guidance from the
        <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Office of the Australian Information Commissioner<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
        about whether it can consider your complaint.
      </p>

      <h3>Changes to this notice</h3>
      <p>
        We may update this notice when the website or our information-handling practices change. The date above
        identifies the latest revision.
      </p>

      <h2>Terms of use</h2>

      <h3>What a listing is</h3>
      <p>
        The directory helps people discover datasets and contact their custodians. The network does not hold or host
        research data, or grant permission to access it. Each custodian decides who may use their data and on what terms,
        and remains responsible for relevant ethics approvals, participant consent and data access agreements. Inclusion in
        the directory is not an endorsement of a dataset or an individual.
      </p>

      <h3>What you must not submit</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Research data files, or any part of a dataset.</li>
        <li>Participant data, completed consent forms, or anything that could identify a study participant.</li>
        <li>Information about a dataset, a person or a resource that you do not have permission to share.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Accuracy</h3>
      <p>
        The person submitting a listing is responsible for ensuring that the information they provide is accurate,
        complete and kept up to date, and that they have the authority or the custodian’s permission to submit it. The
        network is not responsible for the accuracy or completeness of information supplied by contributors. We may edit
        listings for clarity, and may decline or remove any listing.
      </p>

      <h3>Messages</h3>
      <p>
        Use the contact forms only for genuine enquiries relevant to the network. We may block messages that are
        unsolicited marketing, abusive or automated.
      </p>

      <h3>News and events posts</h3>
      <p>
        The person posting is responsible for the accuracy of the item and for having permission to share it. Study
        recruitment posts must have current ethics approval, show the approval number and approving committee, and direct
        people to the study’s own page. The network does not recruit participants or collect their details. We may edit,
        decline or remove any post.
      </p>

      <h3>Members and resources</h3>
      <p>
        Members agree to the <a href={withBase('/code-of-conduct/')}>member code of conduct</a>, including keeping
        members-only resources within the network.
      </p>

      <h3>No warranty</h3>
      <p>
        We provide this website as is, and do not guarantee that listings or resources are complete, accurate, current or
        suitable for any purpose.
      </p>

      <h3>Changes</h3>
      <p>We may update these terms. The date at the top of this page shows when they last changed.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
